Spec: Day dialog

Purpose:
  Admin-only editing of a single day. A `<dialog>` modal lets the admin add or edit a Holiday or a Lesson, and HTMX
  swaps the updated day cell into the page without a reload. Orchestrates ../realizations/realizations.sdd,
  ../lessons/lessons.sdd and ../holidays/holidays.sdd services, so it owns a view.py and routes.py only.

Owns:
  ./view.py
  ./routes.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../auth/auth.sdd
  ../realizations/realizations.sdd
  ../lessons/lessons.sdd
  ../holidays/holidays.sdd

Must:
  Clicking a day cell opens a `<dialog>` for the admin and does nothing for unauthenticated visitors.
  The dialog can add a Holiday (a title) or a Lesson (choosing a CourseRealization, then a time, a topic and notes)
  for the clicked date.
  Submitting the form is an HTMX request that responds with the updated day cell, which replaces the old one in the
  DOM without a page reload.
  The swapped cell keeps the appearance required by the view that contains it.
  Submissions from non-admin sessions are rejected by the ../auth/auth.sdd guard.

Scenario: Admin adds a lesson
  Given the admin is logged in and views the semester view
  When the admin clicks a day row, chooses a course realization, enters a time, a topic and notes and submits
  Then the dialog closes and the day row shows a new colored square without a page reload

Scenario: Visitor clicks a day
  Given the visitor is not logged in
  When the visitor clicks a day row
  Then no dialog opens

Tasks:
  [ ] Implement the dialog and the holiday form with the HTMX cell swap
  [ ] Implement the lesson form
  [ ] Implement editing of existing entries
